@startuml Basic Strategy Pattern

' Define the styles
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam classBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam stereotypeCBackgroundColor #e9ecef

' Title
title Basic Strategy Pattern - Core Structure

' Strategy Interface
interface Strategy <<interface>> {
  +execute(): void
}

' Concrete Strategies
class ConcreteStrategyA <<ConcreteStrategy>> {
  +execute(): void
}

class ConcreteStrategyB <<ConcreteStrategy>> {
  +execute(): void
}

class ConcreteStrategyC <<ConcreteStrategy>> {
  +execute(): void
}

' Context
class Context <<Context>> {
  -strategy: Strategy
  +setStrategy(strategy: Strategy): void
  +executeStrategy(): void
}

' Relationships
Strategy <|.. ConcreteStrategyA
Strategy <|.. ConcreteStrategyB
Strategy <|.. ConcreteStrategyC

Context o--> "1" Strategy : uses

Context ..> Strategy : delegates to >

' Pattern component notes
note right of Strategy
  <b>Strategy Interface</b>
  Declares common interface for
  all supported algorithms.

  Context uses this interface to
  call algorithm defined by
  ConcreteStrategy.
end note

note left of ConcreteStrategyA
  <b>Concrete Strategy A</b>
  Implements algorithm using
  Strategy interface.

  Each concrete strategy provides
  a different implementation of
  the algorithm.
end note

note left of Context
  <b>Context</b>
  • Maintains reference to Strategy object
  • Configured with ConcreteStrategy object
  • Delegates algorithm to Strategy
  • May define interface to let Strategy
    access its data

  <b>Key Method:</b>
  executeStrategy() calls
  strategy.execute()
end note
' Legend positioned to the right

note right of Context
  <b>Strategy Pattern Core Components:</b>

  <b>Strategy:</b> Common interface for all
  supported algorithms/behaviors.

  <b>ConcreteStrategy:</b> Implements the
  algorithm using Strategy interface.

  <b>Context:</b> Configured with ConcreteStrategy
  object and delegates to Strategy interface.

  <b>Key Benefits:</b>
  • Defines family of algorithms
  • Encapsulates each algorithm
  • Makes algorithms interchangeable
  • Lets algorithm vary independently
    from clients that use it

  <b>Intent:</b>
  Define a family of algorithms,
  encapsulate each one, and make
  them interchangeable.
end note

@enduml